{"name":"Heart of Gold","hex":"#9d7f4c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"heart of gold","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind, compassionate, or caring attitude; kindheartedness; a person with those qualities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heart_of_gold"}],"entries":[{"title":"A Heart of Gold","blocks":[{"text":"A Heart of Gold is a 1915 American silent romantic drama short film directed by Tom Ricketts starring Harry von Meter, Reaves Eason, Louise Lester, Jack Richardson, and Vivian Rich."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Heart_of_Gold","wikidata":"Q16251107"},{"title":"Heart of Gold (1923 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Heart of Gold is a 1923 Spanish silent film directed by Manuel Noriega and starring Irene Alba, Juan Bonafé and Elisa Ruiz Romero. It was remade in 1941 under the same title."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heart_of_Gold_(1923_film)","wikidata":"Q5669570"},{"title":"Heart of Gold (Neil Young song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Heart of Gold\" is a song by Canadian singer-songwriter Neil Young. From his fourth studio album Harvest (1972), it is Young's only U.S. No. 1 single. In Canada, it reached No. 1 on the RPM national singles chart for the first time on April 8, 1972, on which date Young held the top spot on both the singles and albums charts, and No. 1 again on May 13. Billboard ranked it as the No. 17 song for 1972."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Heart_of_gold_neil_young_Greek_single.png/330px-Heart_of_gold_neil_young_Greek_single.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heart_of_Gold_(Neil_Young_song)","wikidata":"Q1592434"},{"title":"Heart","blocks":[{"text":"The heart is a muscular organ found in humans and other animals. This organ pumps blood through the blood vessels. The heart and blood vessels together make up the circulatory system. The pumped blood carries oxygen and nutrients to the tissue, while carrying metabolic waste such as carbon dioxide to the lungs. In humans, the heart is approximately the size of a closed fist and is located between the lungs, in the middle compartment of the chest, called the mediastinum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png/330px-Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heart","wikidata":"Q1072"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b7/Humhrt2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b7/Humhrt2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Human heart during an autopsy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHumhrt2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/CG_Heart.gif/500px-CG_Heart.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/CG_Heart.gif/500px-CG_Heart.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Computer-generated animation of a beating human heart","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACG_Heart.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Heart_near.png/500px-Heart_near.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Heart_near.png/500px-Heart_near.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The human heart is in the middle of the thorax, with its apex pointing to the left.[14]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHeart_near.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Heart_disecci